# Frontend Design Standards

> These rules ensure every UI we build matches the design source exactly and uses design tokens consistently. For code organization, file size limits, ES6, constants, and utils rules — see `14-frontend-code-organization.md`. For token values, see `.claude/style/design-tokens.md`.

---

## 1. Design Tokens — ALWAYS use tokens, NEVER hardcode values

### Tailwind classes only — no arbitrary values

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT — use Tailwind scale
<div className="p-4 text-sm text-gray-500 rounded-lg">

// ❌ WRONG — arbitrary values are forbidden
<div className="p-[13px] text-[13px] text-[#6b6b6b] rounded-[6px]">
```

**Banned patterns** — never write these:
- `p-[Xpx]`, `m-[Xpx]`, `w-[Xpx]`, `h-[Xpx]` — use spacing tokens
- `text-[#hex]` — use color tokens
- `bg-[#hex]` — use color tokens
- `rounded-[Xpx]` — use radius tokens
- `text-[Xpx]` — use font-size tokens
- `border-[#hex]` — use color tokens

### Exception: fixed layout dimensions from your design source

The **only** acceptable arbitrary values are for exact design-specified layout widths/heights that have no Tailwind equivalent and appear exactly once:
```tsx
// Acceptable — exact pixel dimension on a layout container, documented inline
<div className="w-[384px]">   {/* Design: side panel = 384px */}
```
If the same dimension appears more than once → add it to your Tailwind theme as a named token. Also add it to `lib/constants/` as a named constant.

### Token reference

Always check `.claude/style/design-tokens.md` before choosing any color, spacing, radius, or font size. If a value from your design source is not in the token file, **add it to the Tailwind theme** (`@theme` in Tailwind v4) — do not use a one-off arbitrary value.

### No duplicate tokens

Before adding a new token, grep for existing tokens with the same or similar value. One value = one token name:
```
// ❌ WRONG — two tokens, same hex
gray-border: #E6E6E6
border-light: #E6E6E6

// ✅ CORRECT — one canonical token used everywhere
gray-100: #E6E6E6
```

